A||||18||rah||Are Fieros Collectibles?
Z||000000||rah||08-30-99||01:12 AM||||Now it's silly to ask a forum of Fieros how common they are nowadays, but I am wondering how much people see of them?<p>I see maybe 1 per week tops in the Minneapolis, MN area.  And to be completely honest, my 84 has the best body condition of any of them.  <p>The car collector museums I've been to all seem to have at least one Fiero, usually an early one, along with otherc cars going way back and newer, but rarer ones like the DeLoreans.<p>When I found out I was gonna have to invest the car's value or more into brakes recently family was questioning how worth it it was, if the car should be let go of or junked.  I was told by the boys at the Pontiac dealer service area they considered them rare, unique, collectibles, and mine to be the best one they've had in.  <p>So, what's everyone's opinion?
Z||000001||Gokart||08-30-99||03:07 AM||||I doubt Fieros will ever be a high priced collectable like a Delorean, but will always be eye candy for anyone who appreciates a beautiful, rare car. Just yesterday I caught myself starring at a restored AMC Pacer parked at Autozone! I hated these cars back when they were all over the place but this one for some reason this one looked good! Our cars have been and always will be beautiful and hopefully someday will be a gem to own, but even if it never is, my GT will always be one to me! I only see about 2 other Fieros a week myself and of course my looks best! Theres your "unbiased" forum member opinion!
Z||000002||Patrick||08-30-99||03:28 AM||||<br>Gokart, you saw an AMC Pacer and you liked it?<p>You need counseling.<IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-30-99||07:29 AM||||Then I guess I need mind-altering drugs, because I saw a nearly-mint V8 Gremlin at a car show and thought it was cool!<p>I don't think Fieros will ever bring big bucks, but they will certainly be collectible in the same way that a Corvair, MGB, or '65 Mustang coupe is collectible.  We may be there already.
Z||000004||lowCG||08-30-99||02:13 PM||||Hey! Was that a "Levis Gremlin"?<br>Now that's a collectors item.<br>Corvair status is what we're headed for in my humble opinion.<br>My cars never even come close to being anything of "collector's" value;they've had too much changed/too many miles,but,hey, I drive the heck out of my cars,after all that's what they're for.
Z||000005||Silver Bullet||08-30-99||02:18 PM||||I would reccomend fixing it because even if they aren't collectors items, their still a hell of a lot of fun, and they turn alot of heads.  Hope ya make the right decision.
Z||000006||Patrick||08-30-99||02:51 PM||||<br>Chadman, I've seen Glemlins also that looked pretty good, but the Pacer is in a class all of it's own!<p> <IMG SRC="http://www.javelinamx.com/Pacer/8.jpg"> <p>Yuck...<p>
