Z||000008||mwbackus||08-30-99||04:18 PM||||As far as the fiero being collectable, I would say you have to look at some obvious facts.  The production numbers were somewhat high, and therefore it will be a longer period of time before values will start to increase considerably.  Supply/demand is a very big factor, the kitcar industries effects on this it should help, but there are still many low mileage cars available.  At any rate, I would say that only the lowest mileage cars (&lt; 20k) will actually see any real large appreciation, and that will probably take another 8 to 15 yrs.  Kinda counts my 108k formula out of that scenario. :-(<p>Mike
