Z||000017||Ozzy||09-01-99||09:43 PM||||I almost lost my 'cookies" lookin' @ that ugly sucker of a...... Car??.<p>Collectors item?? Nah. Fun Item...ubetchya!<br>I'm with mwbackus on this. Only the low miles, genuine article, warts 'n' all will fit the bill "collectable". <p>As to if it's worth throwing the time and money into...Depends how much you dig the machine. I've been with plenty of women who I threw LOTS more money at and they don't even stack up! (except my new wife...she's a sweety, luvs the Fiero and lets me spend as much money on it as I wan't! What more do you want??)<p>Anyway, I new nothing of Fiero's 2 months ago and was looking for a commuter to keep the miles off my new truck. I saw this '88 coupe and thought hmmmm looks kinda kewl don't it?? I think that was the begining of a new kinda relationship. I kinda fell for this car. Must have 'cause if I had a jap rig or similiar and I had to work on it as much as this thing I would set fire to it!!<br>I would not wan't to own one if I had to pay a shop $60.00 and hour to fix evrything.<p>If you DIG it, DO it!!<p>Ozzy
Z||000018||Ozzy||09-02-99||07:45 AM||||BTW, avoid the 'EXPERT' advice mostly given by people who can't even spell Fiero let alone have even driven or OWNED one. You know - goes something like this: "OOOOOOhhhhh a Fiero. Yeah they're a death trap. You'll likley spontaeously combust in one of those". You will be driving down the road one day and a BIG fire breathing monster will loom up out of the engine bay and reach it's firey arm in the window and tear your head off and bowl it down the highway laughing all the while!!!"<p>It is my opinion that while these little treasures do have some obviouse common problems, they are still a decent design concept. Mechanically they are fine so long as you PAY ATTENTION. If there is a problem, fix it! Most of the dead soldiers I see along the side of the road are generally owned by people who just drive 'em and expect the thing to fix itself. Just like a fine woman needs regular attention, so to does our lil' friend the Fiero!<p>Sorry, I get a "little" carried away sometimes.<p>Ozzy<br>
